18. Interview Questions
=======================

Q1. What is a class template?

A generic class that works with multiple data types using one implementation.

---------------------------------------------------------

Q2. Difference between function template and class template?

Function Template
-----------------

• Generic function

• Type often deduced automatically

• Compiler generates function

---------------------------------

Class Template
--------------

• Generic class

• Type must usually be specified explicitly

• Compiler generates class

---------------------------------------------------------

Q3. Why does Box<int> require <int>?

Unlike function templates, class template arguments are generally not deduced
during object creation (before C++17 CTAD).

---------------------------------------------------------

Q4. What is template instantiation?

The compiler generates an actual class from a template for a specific type.

---------------------------------------------------------

Q5. Can class templates have multiple template parameters?

Yes.

Example

template<typename T, typename U>

---------------------------------------------------------

Q6. Can class templates have default template arguments?

Yes.

Example

template<typename T = int>

---------------------------------------------------------

Q7. Can class templates have static members?

Yes.

Each template instantiation has its own copy of static members.

---------------------------------------------------------

Q8. Can constructors be templates?

Yes.

A class template can also contain template constructors.

---------------------------------------------------------

Q9. Why are class template implementations kept in header files?

Because the compiler needs the complete implementation during template
instantiation.

---------------------------------------------------------

Q10. Are STL containers class templates?

Yes.

Examples

vector<T>

list<T>

map<K,V>

set<T>

queue<T>

stack<T>

---------------------------------------------------------

Q11. Can class templates be inherited?

Yes.

Example

template<typename T>
class Base
{
};

template<typename T>
class Derived : public Base<T>
{
};

---------------------------------------------------------

Q12. Can a class template contain normal (non-template) member functions?

Yes.

Not every member function needs to be a template.

---------------------------------------------------------

19. Common Mistakes
==================

❌ Forgetting <T> while defining member functions outside the class.

Incorrect

Box::getValue()

Correct

Box<T>::getValue()

---------------------------------

❌ Implementing templates only in .cpp files.

---------------------------------

❌ Assuming static members are shared across all template types.

Counter<int>::count

and

Counter<double>::count

are different variables.

---------------------------------

❌ Forgetting to specify template arguments.

Incorrect

Box b;

Correct

Box<int> b;

(CTAD in C++17 is an exception.)

---------------------------------------------------------

20. Quick Revision
==================

✓ Class templates create generic classes.

✓ Defined using

template<typename T>

✓ Compiler generates class during instantiation.

✓ Multiple template parameters are supported.

✓ Default template parameters are supported.

✓ Non-type template parameters are supported.

✓ Static members are separate for each template instantiation.

✓ Template implementations are generally placed in header files.

✓ STL containers like vector, list, map, queue and stack are class templates.

✓ Class templates provide compile-time polymorphism.

